 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DezdxAxh1rL/",
 "title": "Low-effort way to look more senior at work",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "This video shares a simple communication habit to help you look more senior and valuable at work. The creator advises asking yourself three specific questions before communicating anything so you can be a source of clarity instead of confusion.",
 "key_points": [
  "At work, people are either sources of confusion or sources of clarity, and you want to be a source of clarity.",
  "Before communicating anything, ask yourself three questions.",
  "Question 1: How much detail does this person or group need?",
  "Question 2: Why does it matter to them?",
  "Question 3: What am I expecting them to do with the information?",
  "Filtering your communication through these three questions naturally leads people to a state of clarity."
 ],
 "content": "Low-effort way to look more senior. This is a small simple work that will have people seeing you as more competent, more senior, more valuable. And this goes for people with any type of job. At work there are people who are sources of confusion and people who are sources of clarity. You obviously want to be the latter. When people walk away from an interaction with you, you want them feeling like they understand things better. And here's one thing that will help you be a source of clarity. Before communicating anything, ask yourself three questions. How much detail does this person or group need? Why does it matter to them? What am I expecting them to do with the information? If you filter your communication through those three questions, you'll naturally lead people to a state of clarity. Screen text: Low-effort way to look more senior. Want more simple, practical advice to accelerate your career? Follow along.",
 "status": "done",
